# B-0 FAILS as pre-registered: no nonzero AIE-tile counter value. Every other condition holds.
#   - xdp_aie_profile_plugin.dll loaded by configuration alone.
#   - It configured all 16 cores through XDP_KERNEL ("Reserved 4 counters ... heat_map", "Successfully
#     scheduled AIE Profile Setup instruction buffer") and read 64 counters back ("Profile Poll").
#   - The outputs are bit-equal and the xmodel did not recompile.
# Answered: (1) XDP_KERNEL configure and register read-back work on this firmware.
# Not answered: (2) whether counters survive a DPU_PDI run, and (3) which tiles are active. The cores
# computed (the outputs are right), yet every counter reads 0. That is UNEXPLAINED. Three candidates, none
# ruled out:
#   - the PDI 2 load re-initialises the core modules after XDP armed them at xclbin load;
#   - the end-of-run poll lands after a context teardown that reset them;
#   - the heat_map events (28, 22, 37, 32) do not count in this configuration.
# Consequence for Route B: arm after a warm-up DPU_PDI_2 run, in our own context, as the plan already says.
